--TEST--
`Core\Socket::upgrade` refuses the two entry spellings ADR 0006 § *Decision* forbids, at `rule:concurrency/an-upgrade-is-spawn-shaped`'s second site and with that ADR's own diagnostic
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Chat {
    public static function run(string $room): void {}
}

string $room = "lobby";

// `rule:security/isolate-shares-nothing` refuses an anonymous function because the same syntax one keyword away
// in `spawn worker` *does* capture its enclosing scope, and an isolate shares
// nothing but compiled code -- so one spelling with two meanings is what the
// refusal exists to prevent. This one reads `$room`, which is exactly the
// capture that could not cross.
Core\Socket::upgrade(fn(): string => $room);

// The other spelling, and the one no rule phrased over *types* could tell from
// the accepted `Chat::run(...)`: `$entry` holds what that reference produces
// and has the same type, so what separates them is that the compiler can see
// the function in one and not in the other.
callable $entry = Chat::run(...);
Core\Socket::upgrade($entry);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0802]: a `Core\Socket::upgrade` entry is a path or a static method
%A
error[E0802]: a `Core\Socket::upgrade` entry is a path or a static method
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
